    "turn_idx": 4,
    "turn_text": "That's a great question. I think that we're currently, so we passed that border security bill. So we took priority number one. We built an incredibly successful border security bill. many different actions that we took under those three categories I just mentioned. And we got that passed about, I think it was probably six weeks ago. Now we're diving into holding Secretary Mayorkas and President Biden accountable for just what that open border has done to America. And I think the fact that 12,000 Chinese nationals have come across our southern border, the sector chiefs have told us that known Military age men with ties to the PLA have just been released into the country as a part of the asylum process. I think that's not getting enough attention. I think the fentanyl deaths not getting enough attention. I think the real crux of the problem for me is that Secretary of America's just thinks he can disregard the laws passed by Congress, and a Cabinet Secretary, nowhere in the Constitution, does it say that they get to just pick and choose which laws they're going to enforce. I find that as a real threat to the Constitution itself, to the foundation of our government, which is separation of powers. Our founders were brilliant. They recognize that when you concentrate power into the hands of a few, and in the case of a monarch one, you get tyranny. And so they spread power out between three separate branches of government, and of course, between federal, state, and local. That 10th Amendment's pretty clear. If it's not enumerated in the Constitution, it belongs to the states. So this Secretary has just totally disregarded the founding concept of our entire government. He's ignoring the laws passed by Congress. I don't think anyone's really talking about that. And we should be.",
