    "turn_text": "Yeah, I mean, when Finland and Sweden decided to join NATO, that is a huge defeat for Putin from a strategic standpoint. The benefit for the United States, of course, is Finland and Norway have, Norway has the access But those are Arctic countries. And the amazing thing about it is now seven of the countries that border are allied with the United States. So this conquest of the Arctic becomes a huge win for us to have them join NATO. In terms of what it means for Russia, clearly the Finns have a huge border with Russia. And to have an NATO country there, that adds to the security of the alliance itself. And I think we can put him from a strategic perspective. But he is so far back on his heels from his failure in Ukraine, I'm not sure it's a near-term impact, it's more of a long-term impact.",
